---
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro'
import Logo from '@/components/ui/Logo.astro'
import Footer from '@/components/layout/Footer.astro'
---

<Layout
  title="Why This Project Exists — Progress Tab"
  description="A personal story about tracking meaningful progress and building lasting habits."
>
  <div class="min-h-screen bg-background text-foreground">

    <!-- Top nav -->
    <div class="sticky top-0 z-50 border-b border-border/50 bg-background/80 backdrop-blur-sm">
      <div class="mx-auto flex max-w-container items-center justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-4 sm:px-8 lg:px-12">
        <a
          href="/"
          class="group inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-muted transition-colors hover:text-foreground"
        >
          <svg
            width="16"
            height="16"
            viewBox="0 0 16 16"
            fill="none"
            class="transition-transform duration-200 group-hover:-translate-x-0.5"
          >
            <path
              d="M10 12L6 8l4-4"
              stroke="currentColor"
              stroke-width="1.5"
              stroke-linecap="round"
              stroke-linejoin="round"
            />
          </svg>
          Back
        </a>
        <Logo />
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Content -->
    <main class="mx-auto max-w-[42rem] px-5 pb-24 pt-16 sm:px-8 sm:pt-20">

      <!-- Header -->
      <div class="mb-14 animate-fade-up" style="animation-delay: 0.05s">
        <div class="mb-5 inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full border border-momentum/25 bg-momentum/5 px-3.5 py-1.5">
          <span class="h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-momentum"></span>
          <span class="text-xs font-medium tracking-wide text-momentum">Origin story</span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="font-display text-hero font-display leading-none text-foreground">
          Why this<br />project exists
        </h1>
      </div>

      <!-- Body -->
      <article class="prose-story animate-fade-up" style="animation-delay: 0.15s">

        <p class="lead">
          A few years ago, I realized something.
        </p>

        <p>
          Social media, video games, and other forms of instant entertainment were enjoyable in the
          moment, but they rarely left anything behind. After winning a game, my life was exactly
          the same as before. A few months later, a new version would come out, and all those
          achievements would become meaningless.
        </p>

        <p>
          Social media felt similar. I could spend hours reading, commenting, and following other
          people's lives, but when I closed the app, I had no new skills, no deeper understanding
          of the world, and no meaningful progress in my own life.
        </p>

        <p>That led me to a simple question:</p>

        <blockquote>
          What if I spent more time on activities that actually left something behind?
        </blockquote>

        <p>
          At first, that meant books and films. Not just entertainment, but works that could teach
          me something, challenge my perspective, or help me better understand the world around me.
        </p>

        <p>
          Over time, I realized that I wanted more than knowledge for its own sake. I wanted to
          improve my life in a meaningful way. That required skills, opportunities, and resources.
          As a result, I became interested in topics like finance, self-education, and professional
          development.
        </p>

        <p>
          Very quickly, I noticed that the deepest understanding often came from books. Articles,
          videos, and podcasts were useful, but books allowed me to explore subjects in far greater
          depth.
        </p>

        <p>The problem was that I had no reading habit.</p>

        <p>
          Reading felt slow. My attention would drift. I got tired quickly and often lost
          motivation to continue. Most importantly, the progress felt too small to matter.
        </p>

        <p>So instead of asking myself how to read more, I started asking a different question:</p>

        <blockquote>How can I avoid quitting?</blockquote>

        <p>
          I needed a simple system that would help me stay consistent, even on days when I had no
          motivation, energy, or desire to continue.
        </p>

        <div class="callout">
          <p>
            The solution was surprisingly simple. I created a spreadsheet and started tracking how
            many pages I read each day. I gave myself only one rule:
            <strong>read at least one page.</strong>
          </p>
        </div>

        <p>
          One page sounds insignificant, but it was enough to get me started. And once I started,
          I often ended up reading much more than I had planned.
        </p>

        <p>Weeks turned into months. The spreadsheet kept growing.</p>

        <p>
          At the same time, my concentration improved. I became a better reader. Complex topics
          became easier to understand.
        </p>

        <p>But the most important benefit appeared on the days when I wanted to quit.</p>

        <p>
          Whenever I looked at the spreadsheet, I didn't just see numbers. I saw evidence of the
          work I had already put in. Months of small daily actions became visible.
        </p>

        <p>That's when I learned something important.</p>

        <blockquote>
          Instant entertainment provides immediate rewards. Meaningful activities work differently.
          They can genuinely improve your life, but the progress is often so gradual that it's
          difficult to notice from day to day.
        </blockquote>

        <p>
          When progress is invisible, it's easy to believe that nothing is happening. And when it
          feels like nothing is happening, it's easy to quit.
        </p>

        <p class="highlight-line">Tracking changed that. It made slow progress visible.</p>

        <p>
          Over time, however, I discovered a flaw in my system. Measuring pages wasn't always
          fair. Twenty pages of a novel and twenty pages of a technical book require completely
          different levels of effort and focus.
        </p>

        <p>So I started looking for a more universal way to measure progress.</p>

        <p>The answer was time.</p>

        <p>
          Time works across almost everything. Reading, learning a language, exercising, building a
          side project, studying, or simply spending time reflecting. If you're consistently
          investing time into something meaningful, you're moving forward.
        </p>

        <p class="section-break">That idea eventually became this project.</p>

        <p>
          Its purpose is not to make people work harder or achieve more in less time.
        </p>

        <p>Its purpose is much simpler.</p>

        <div class="callout callout-momentum">
          <p>
            I wanted to create a tool that helps people see their own consistency. A tool that
            reminds them how far they've already come when progress feels invisible.
          </p>
        </div>

        <p>Because meaningful change rarely happens overnight.</p>

        <p>
          More often, it comes from small actions repeated over long periods of time. And when
          those actions go unnoticed, they're easy to abandon.
        </p>

        <p class="closing">When they become visible, they're much easier to continue.</p>

      </article>

    </main>

    <Footer />
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .prose-story {
    color: hsl(0 0% 87%);
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .prose-story p {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .prose-story p.lead {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: hsl(0 0% 98%);
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin-bottom: 1.75rem;
  }

  .prose-story blockquote {
    margin: 2rem 0;
    padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
    border-left: 3px solid hsl(160 65% 55%);
    background: hsl(160 65% 55% / 0.05);
    border-radius: 0 0.5rem 0.5rem 0;
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    font-style: italic;
    color: hsl(0 0% 96%);
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .prose-story .callout {
    margin: 2.25rem 0;
    padding: 1.5rem 1.75rem;
    background: hsl(240 8% 7%);
    border: 1px solid hsl(240 4% 16%);
    border-radius: 0.75rem;
  }

  .prose-story .callout p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    color: hsl(0 0% 92%);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .prose-story .callout.callout-momentum {
    border-color: hsl(160 65% 55% / 0.3);
    background: hsl(160 65% 55% / 0.06);
  }

  .prose-story .callout.callout-momentum p {
    color: hsl(160 65% 85%);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
  }

  .prose-story strong {
    color: hsl(0 0% 98%);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .prose-story .highlight-line {
    color: hsl(0 0% 98%);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
  }

  .prose-story .section-break {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    padding-top: 3rem;
    border-top: 1px solid hsl(240 4% 16%);
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: hsl(0 0% 98%);
  }

  .prose-story .closing {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: hsl(160 65% 75%);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
</style>
